# SABOTAGE: the gen.app BORN-ARMED emission — the generated WEB file set no longer emits
# `test/flood_guard_armed_test.exs`, so a generated vertical gets the arming line in its
# `test/test_helper.exs` (the `[MOD]` swap, untouched here) with NOTHING that asserts it is armed
# AND biting. Losing that line then goes silent again in every generated app: unarmed, the suite
# still passes and an unpinned flood only FLAKES later, when a wall-clock window boundary
# (`div(now, window)`) resets the counter mid-count.
#
# The claim it refutes is `templates_parity_test`'s born-armed assertion, which is checked against
# the RENDERED output rather than the golden — so this patch flips it even though the golden file
# for the tripwire is still on disk and unchanged. The second named failure is the file-set
# assertion in `gen_app_test`, which is the same emission seen from the generator's own menu.
#
# NOT TOUCHED, deliberately: the template file itself, the arming line in the emitted test helper,
# and the headless set — whose RED half (no `samen_web` dep, so it must emit NEITHER artifact) stays
# green, because this removes the tripwire from the WEB set only.
#
# The `defp flood_guard_armed_test/0` this leaves unused draws one compile warning; the replay runs
# `mix test` (not `--warnings-as-errors`), so the warning is confined to the reverted replay — the
# precedent 329 set for the same reason.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/templates_parity_test.exs test/gen_app_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: every generated web app is BORN ARMED
# MUST_FAIL: web-only file set = the headless paths
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/gen/templates.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/gen/templates.ex
@@ -262,10 +262,6 @@
       {"lib/<%= otp_app %>_web/layouts.ex", layouts_ex()},
       {"lib/<%= otp_app %>_web/page_controller.ex", page_controller_ex()},
       {"lib/<%= otp_app %>_web/error_html.ex", error_html_ex()},
-      # The framework flood-guard TRIPWIRE for the arming line the web test helper carries: a
-      # generated host is BORN armed AND self-verifying (delete the `arm!()` line and THIS
-      # emitted test fails loudly). The probe it calls is samen_web's — never re-emitted.
-      {"test/flood_guard_armed_test.exs", flood_guard_armed_test()}
     ]
 
     base ++ web_new
